      "link": null,
      "locked": true,
      "customData": {
        "title": "The app calls one agent",
        "description": "The intended native runtime route is a signed-in user in a Managed Runtime app calling a published standard-harness Copilot Studio agent through its generated ExecuteCopilotAsyncV2 service. The agent's Invoker-mode Fabric IQ tool reads the bound ontology as that user; its Invoker-mode Foundry IQ tool retrieves document evidence through that user's Search connection. Agent readers access and disabled generic grounding are required. Responses and follow-up messages stay in the same user's conversation. Prove the connection challenge, live answer, follow-up and second-user denial/isolation separately; hosted deployment is also separate. The connector has a 120-second limit. The Foundry Agent Service connector is a different, currently blocked Managed Runtime route.",
        "role": "page"
      },
      "index": "a0"
    },
